📘 Deep State Analysis Tool (DSAT)
🧠 Objective

To continuously monitor application health, detect abnormal behavior from logs/processes, and take automated corrective actions based on defined severity and scope.

1️⃣ System Architecture (High Level)
[Application] 
     ↓
[Log Files / Process Monitoring]
     ↓
[Bash Monitoring Engine]
     ↓
[Decision Engine (Rules + Severity)]
     ↓
[Action Engine]
     ↓
[Logging → DB → Dashboard (future)]
2️⃣ Requirements Definition
🔹 2.1 Application Details

Define for each application:

Application Name
Binary/Service Path
Process Name
Config Path

Example (config file):

APP_NAME="freeswitch"
APP_PROCESS="freeswitch"
APP_START_CMD="systemctl start freeswitch"
APP_STOP_CMD="systemctl stop freeswitch"
APP_RESTART_CMD="systemctl restart freeswitch"
APP_PATH="/usr/bin/freeswitch"
🔹 2.2 Log File Definitions

Define logs to monitor:

LOG_FILES=(
  "/var/log/freeswitch/freeswitch.log"
  "/var/log/app/error.log"
)

Define patterns:

ERROR_PATTERNS=(
  "CRITICAL"
  "ERROR"
  "Segmentation fault"
  "connection refused"
)
🔹 2.3 Scope of Work (Automation Boundaries)

This is very important for production safety.

Allowed Actions:
Action	Condition
Start	Process not running
Stop	High failure rate
Restart	Hang / repeated errors
Alert only	Unknown issues
NOT Allowed (initial phase):
Config changes ❌
DB modifications ❌
Bulk cleanup ❌
🔹 2.4 Severity Definition
Severity	Condition	Action	SLA
P1 (Critical)	App down / crash	Restart + Alert	Immediate
P2 (Major)	Errors > threshold	Restart	5 min
P3 (Minor)	Warning patterns	Alert only	15 min
P4 (Info)	Normal logs	No action	-
🔹 2.5 Incident States
1. DETECTED
2. ACTION_TRIGGERED
3. FIXED
4. ESCALATED
5. UNRESOLVED
3️⃣ Monitoring Logic (Core Engine)
🔹 3.1 Process Check
check_process() {
    pgrep -x "$APP_PROCESS" > /dev/null
    if [ $? -ne 0 ]; then
        echo "Process not running"
        return 1
    fi
    return 0
}
🔹 3.2 Log Analysis
scan_logs() {
    for file in "${LOG_FILES[@]}"; do
        for pattern in "${ERROR_PATTERNS[@]}"; do
            grep -i "$pattern" "$file" | tail -n 5
        done
    done
}
🔹 3.3 Error Threshold Logic
ERROR_COUNT=$(grep -i "ERROR" /var/log/app.log | wc -l)

if [ "$ERROR_COUNT" -gt 50 ]; then
    SEVERITY="P2"
fi
4️⃣ Action Engine
🔹 4.1 Restart Logic
restart_app() {
    echo "Restarting application..."
    $APP_RESTART_CMD
}
🔹 4.2 Start/Stop Logic
start_app() {
    $APP_START_CMD
}

stop_app() {
    $APP_STOP_CMD
}
🔹 4.3 Decision Engine
if ! check_process; then
    SEVERITY="P1"
    start_app
elif [ "$ERROR_COUNT" -gt 50 ]; then
    SEVERITY="P2"
    restart_app
else
    SEVERITY="P3"
fi
5️⃣ Alerting System
🔹 5.1 Email Alert (Basic)
send_alert() {
    SUBJECT="[$SEVERITY] Issue detected in $APP_NAME"
    echo "Issue detected at $(date)" | mail -s "$SUBJECT" team@example.com
}
🔹 5.2 Escalation Logic
if [ "$SEVERITY" == "P1" ]; then
    send_alert "L1"
    sleep 300
    send_alert "L2"
fi
